<ul>
 <li><span>Polarion will then have two entries of the user. One with FID an=
d a new one with username.&nbsp;</span><span>&nbsp;</span></li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li><span>In this scenario, to retain the history of the user, AO team wil=
l map the new account to the existing account.</span><span>&nbsp;</span></l=
i>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li><span>AO support will ask the user to login to Polarion with a new use=
r ID (</span><strong><span>firstname.lastname)</span></strong><span> and wi=
ndow password.</span><span>&nbsp;</span></li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li><span>If still the user is not able to update password for FME\usernam=
e, then AO Team will reach out to the </span><a class=3D"external-link" hre=
f=3D"mailto:globalDTIservicedesk@freseniusmedicalcare.com" rel=3D"nofollow"=
><span>Global DTI ServiceDesk</span></a><span> for new password.</span><spa=
n>&nbsp;</span></li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li><span>AO support will ask the user to login to Polarion with new passw=
ord received from DTI Team.</span><span>&nbsp;</span></li>
</ul>
<p><u><strong>Scenario-8 </strong><strong>Inactive AD Account/ AD account l=
ocked / AD account not available:&nbsp;</strong></u></p>
<p><span style=3D"color:#c25100;"><strong>Note:<span style=3D"color:#172b4d=
;"> </span><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">S</span><span style=3D"color:#172=
